-- PROBE-PLAYBOOKS-1 (2026-10-26, charter pillar: autonomy; agent_issues 1000266 BREACH-DOCTOR-1 family PROBE-NEEDED-1; package probe-playbooks).
-- The doctor engine (qnfo-fleet-control 0.52.0, migrations/2026-10-26-breach-doctor.sql) classified its first 40 cases 'unclassified' because only the CODE-MERGE-REFUSED-1 and
-- CODE-LOOP-EXHAUSTED-1 seed rules exist. This file is data for it: 10 playbook rows for the broken closing paths of the PROBE-NEEDED-1 family and of the orphan issues with a known title
-- shape, plus the metrics, failure modes and the one code lever that family needs. No worker.js change (BD_WRITE_TABLES already holds issue_triage, agent_issues and remediation_contracts),
-- so no VERSION bump and no mirror.
-- MEASURED read-only on live qnfo-audit 2026-10-26 11:25Z. The audit of 05:45Z had moved: ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 issue-meta-fold, ISSUE-PROBE-AGENT-1 and sessions drained part of it, so a rule that
-- finds 0 today is kept as the 10-minute second path and the guard (ANTIFRAGILE-1), the role CM-R1 to CM-R5 of the engine migration have.
--   open PROBE-NEEDED-1 19 (15 older than 120 minutes), 4 of them with a probe-review-refused contract on the fleet's own PN probe, 7 for OWNER-TASK or OWNER-NOTE targets, 0 with a closed target;
--   open issues with no live closing path (stricter definition: no active, holding, monitoring or escalated contract that is not a BACKFILL-1 alias or reads close_evidence) 75 older than 60 minutes
--   (198 at the audit), and 84 open issues carry a superseded-at-birth contract.
-- WHAT EACH ROW DOES (hit counts are the trigger_sql run read-only just before this file was written):
--   PN-R1   close a PN whose target has been closed for 30 minutes, with evidence; second path of the hourly ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 workflow          live hits 0 (the 5 the audit named were closed by that workflow)
--   PN-R2   close a PN for an OWNER-TASK/OWNER-NOTE target, SUPERSEDED BY the target, behind a self-releasing gate (control below)           live hits 0 (gate closed: 6 class-C PN events in 24 h, 7 candidates)
--   PN-R3   restore the fleet's own PN probe that PROBE-REVIEW-1 refused (module swap to probe-template-v4-pn, which it skips)               live hits 4 (6 at 10:55Z)
--   PB-R0   restore a contract superseded at birth whose probe measures a real condition                                                      live hits 0 (the 6 METRIC-UNMEASURED-1 contracts 1000384 to 1000389 were restored meanwhile)
--   PB-T1   portfolio-gap template, PB-T3 journey template, PB-T4 metric template, each as a pending (active) row and a green-at-birth (holding, second read 60 minutes later) row
--                                                                                                                                          live hits T1 1, T3 1, T4 2, green forms 0
-- Not here, with the reason. The superseded-at-birth issues without a known title shape are the probe author's: package probe-author-fix, R6. T2 (tool recovery): tool issues already get TOOL-ISSUE-SELFCLOSE-1 (trigger tool_issue_probe_on_supersede), the tool-loop package owns their classification, and the probe
-- reads cloud_ops_events, which the engine's taint rule forbids in an action statement. R4 (alias hardening of rtLivePathProbe and RT_LIVEPATH_ORPHAN_SQL) is code and R6 is the probe author's.
-- R7 (BACKFILL-1 replacement) is the last statement of every template action: the alias is superseded only after the template contract is live. R8 is the green-at-birth form of each template.
-- Every action statement binds ?1 = the issue and touches only its own rows (class issue-<id>, the issue's BACKFILL-1 aliases, the PN's own triage row). Every close writes issue_triage.close_evidence
-- from ids and enum codes through the live close-sync trigger and a failing active contract blocks it. Every row has a revert_sql and a verify_sql that reads ok only when the defect is gone, and the
-- engine's S3 caps apply (a new row runs in measure for 30 minutes, max_per_tick 6 and the global max_actions, 2 failures in 24 hours demote the rule).
-- ORDER: file-name order puts this after 2026-10-26-breach-doctor.sql, which creates breach_playbooks and breach_causes.
-- A replay changes nothing (INSERT OR IGNORE and guarded inserts). decision_log is append-only, so the Rollback keeps its row.
-- REVIEW 2026-10-26 (six blocking findings, all fixed in this file): (1) the code lever's contract is installed on live: the INSERT fires agent_issues_birth_contract_ins and contract_probe_templates_loop_merged then parks the
--   contract as monitoring / probe-template-v2d-loop (qnfo-fleet-control is a live service_registry row), so the UPDATE matches needs-machine-probe, monitoring and superseded and resets verdict, attempts and due time;
--   (2) its closing probe is a code-read of main for the exclusion, not a quiet-day proxy: the filer writes no event when it dedupes against an open PN (live issue_lifecycle holds a 49-hour class-C gap, 2026-10-21 10:11Z to
--   2026-10-23 11:46Z, with the defect present) and it is capped at 12 PN per 1440 minutes; (3) no detector threshold exceeds 120 minutes and every window is stated in minutes (the PN-R2 gate window is 1440 minutes: the filer's own
--   dedupe horizon, not a stuck-item SLA); (4) PB-R0 restores a contract under module breach-doctor-restored so qnfo-cloud-ops PROBE-REVIEW-1 (which skips module LIKE probe-template%) still judges the restored probe;
--   (5) PN-R2 and PB-T4 act on beliefs, so each has a belief_registry row and a belief- probe that can falsify it, and the PN-R2 close_evidence states only what the rule read.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE breach_playbooks SET enabled = 0, mode = 'measure' WHERE rule_id IN ('PN-R1', 'PN-R2', 'PN-R3', 'PB-R0', 'PB-T1', 'PB-T1-green', 'PB-T3', 'PB-T3-green', 'PB-T4', 'PB-T4-green'); UPDATE analytics_metric_triggers SET enabled = 0 WHERE metric_key IN ('orphan_issues_no_live_path', 'probe_author_accept_rate_7d', 'pn_open_over_120m'); UPDATE fleet_crons SET enabled = 0 WHERE name = 'probe-playbooks-metrics-10m'; UPDATE fleet_tasks SET enabled = 0 WHERE id = 'probe-playbooks-metrics'; UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = 'superseded' WHERE class IN ('fm-probe-author-unreachable', 'fm-pn-probe-refused', 'fm-pn-target-closed-open', 'fm-born-superseded-real-probe', 'belief-pn-r2-owner-outcome-unmeasured', 'belief-pb-t4-metric-title-is-about-the-metric'); each applied case stores its own revert_sql in breach_diagnoses (v_breach_diagnosis_current) and the playbook rows stay as the ledger of the engine; the issue BREACH-DOCTOR-1: PN-R2 qnfo-fleet-control stays open until its probe closes it.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO breach_playbooks (rule_id, version, family, cause_class, action_kind, trigger_sql, action_sql, revert_sql, verify_sql, min_ladder, max_per_tick, max_per_day, enabled, mode, note) VALUES
  ('PN-R1', 1, 'PROBE-NEEDED-1', 'target-closed', 'sql', 'SELECT p.id AS issue_id, ''target-closed'' AS subject, json_object(''target_id'', t.id, ''target_status'', t.status, ''lifecycle_id'', COALESCE((SELECT l.id FROM issue_lifecycle l WHERE l.issue_id = t.id AND l.to_status IN (''closed'',''resolved'',''wontfix'') ORDER BY l.id DESC LIMIT 1), 0), ''closed_ts'', COALESCE((SELECT l.ts FROM issue_lifecycle l WHERE l.issue_id = t.id AND l.to_status IN (''closed'',''resolved'',''wontfix'') ORDER BY l.id DESC LIMIT 1), ''none''), ''has_evidence'', COALESCE((SELECT l.has_evidence FROM issue_lifecycle l WHERE l.issue_id = t.id AND l.to_status IN (''closed'',''resolved'',''wontfix'') ORDER BY l.id DESC LIMIT 1), 0)) AS facts_json FROM agent_issues p JOIN agent_issues t ON t.id = CAST(substr(p.title, 23) AS INTEGER) WHERE p.status = ''open'' AND p.source = ''qnfo-fleet-control'' AND p.title LIKE ''PROBE-NEEDED-1: issue-%'' AND p.title = ''PROBE-NEEDED-1: issue-'' || CAST(substr(p.title, 23) AS INTEGER) AND t.status IN (''closed'',''resolved'',''wontfix'') AND COALESCE((SELECT MAX(l.ts) FROM issue_lifecycle l WHERE l.issue_id = t.id AND l.to_status IN (''closed'',''resolved'',''wontfix'')), '''') <= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'',''-30 minutes'') AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_lifecycle l WHERE l.issue_id = t.id AND l.event = ''reopened'' AND l.ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'',''-30 minutes'')) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = p.id AND c.status IN (''active'',''holding'') AND COALESCE(c.last_verdict,'''') IN (''fail'',''vacuous-probe-result'',''probe-error'',''probe-not-machine-executable'',''probe-same-account-host''))', json_array('INSERT INTO issue_triage (issue_id, rc, triage_state, owner, sla_due_at, close_evidence) SELECT p.id, ''breach-doctor:PN-R1'', ''closed'', ''breach-doctor'', datetime(''now''), ''PROBE-NEEDED-1 obsolete: target issue '' || t.id || '' is '' || t.status || '' (issue_lifecycle id '' || COALESCE((SELECT l.id FROM issue_lifecycle l WHERE l.issue_id = t.id AND l.to_status IN (''closed'',''resolved'',''wontfix'') ORDER BY l.id DESC LIMIT 1), 0) || '' at '' || COALESCE((SELECT l.ts FROM issue_lifecycle l WHERE l.issue_id = t.id AND l.to_status IN (''closed'',''resolved'',''wontfix'') ORDER BY l.id DESC LIMIT 1), ''none'') || '', has_evidence '' || COALESCE((SELECT l.has_evidence FROM issue_lifecycle l WHERE l.issue_id = t.id AND l.to_status IN (''closed'',''resolved'',''wontfix'') ORDER BY l.id DESC LIMIT 1), 0) || ''), so the probe this issue asked for has no open subject. Measured by a D1 read of agent_issues and issue_lifecycle at close. Closed by breach-doctor rule PN-R1 from ids and enum codes only.'' FROM agent_issues p JOIN agent_issues t ON t.id = CAST(substr(p.title, 23) AS INTEGER) WHERE p.id = ?1 AND p.status = ''open'' AND p.source = ''qnfo-fleet-control'' AND p.title LIKE ''PROBE-NEEDED-1: issue-%'' AND p.title = ''PROBE-NEEDED-1: issue-'' || CAST(substr(p.title, 23) AS INTEGER) AND t.status IN (''closed'',''resolved'',''wontfix'') AND COALESCE((SELECT MAX(l.ts) FROM issue_lifecycle l WHERE l.issue_id = t.id AND l.to_status IN (''closed'',''resolved'',''wontfix'')), '''') <= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'',''-30 minutes'') AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_lifecycle l WHERE l.issue_id = t.id AND l.event = ''reopened'' AND l.ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'',''-30 minutes'')) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = p.id AND c.status IN (''active'',''holding'') AND COALESCE(c.last_verdict,'''') IN (''fail'',''vacuous-probe-result'',''probe-error'',''probe-not-machine-executable'',''probe-same-account-host'')) ON CONFLICT(issue_id) DO UPDATE SET rc = excluded.rc, triage_state = ''closed'', owner = ''breach-doctor'', close_evidence = excluded.close_evidence', 'UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = ''superseded'', last_verdict = ''superseded:pn-target-closed'', next_due_at = NULL WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND class = ''issue-'' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) AND status IN (''active'',''holding'',''probe-review-refused'') AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues p WHERE p.id = ?1 AND p.status IN (''closed'',''resolved''))'), json_array('UPDATE issue_triage SET triage_state = ''triaged'', close_evidence = NULL WHERE issue_id = ?1', 'UPDATE agent_issues SET status = ''open'', close_channel = NULL, updated_at = CAST(strftime(''%s'',''now'') AS INTEGER) * 1000 WHERE id = ?1 AND status = ''closed''', 'UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = ''active'', last_verdict = NULL, next_due_at = datetime(''now'') WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND class = ''issue-'' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) AND last_verdict = ''superseded:pn-target-closed'''), 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE id = ?1 AND status = ''open'') THEN ''pn-still-open'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues p JOIN agent_issues t ON t.id = CAST(substr(p.title, 23) AS INTEGER) WHERE p.id = ?1 AND t.status = ''open'') THEN ''target-reopened'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed', 'delegated', 6, 25, 1, 'on', 'PROBE-NEEDED-1 issue whose target is closed, resolved or wontfix for 30 minutes without a reopen (hysteresis: issue 100618 flapped three times in 3 h). Closes the PN with close_evidence built from ids and enum codes (agent_issues, issue_lifecycle) and supersedes its own contract. LIVE 2026-10-26 11:25Z: 0 hits. The five the audit named (PN 100476, 100492, 100539, 100602, 1000087) were closed by ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 issue-meta-fold (close_channel workflow:ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 probe-needed-target-not-open) between the audit and this file, so this row is the 10-minute second path and the guard if that hourly workflow stops (ANTIFRAGILE-1), the role CM-R1 to CM-R5 have.');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO breach_playbooks (rule_id, version, family, cause_class, action_kind, trigger_sql, action_sql, revert_sql, verify_sql, min_ladder, max_per_tick, max_per_day, enabled, mode, note) VALUES
  ('PN-R2', 1, 'PROBE-NEEDED-1', 'no-measurable-dod', 'sql', 'SELECT p.id AS issue_id, ''no-measurable-dod'' AS subject, json_object(''target_id'', t.id, ''target_class'', CASE WHEN t.title LIKE ''OWNER-TASK%'' THEN ''owner-task'' ELSE ''owner-note'' END, ''target_priority'', t.priority, ''filer_quiet_24h'', 1) AS facts_json FROM agent_issues p JOIN agent_issues t ON t.id = CAST(substr(p.title, 23) AS INTEGER) WHERE p.status = ''open'' AND p.source = ''qnfo-fleet-control'' AND p.title LIKE ''PROBE-NEEDED-1: issue-%'' AND p.title = ''PROBE-NEEDED-1: issue-'' || CAST(substr(p.title, 23) AS INTEGER) AND t.status = ''open'' AND (t.title LIKE ''OWNER-TASK%'' OR t.title LIKE ''OWNER-NOTE%'') AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_lifecycle gl JOIN agent_issues gq ON gq.id = gl.issue_id JOIN agent_issues gw ON gw.id = CAST(substr(gq.title, 23) AS INTEGER) WHERE gq.title LIKE ''PROBE-NEEDED-1: issue-%'' AND gl.event IN (''opened'',''reopened'') AND gl.ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'',''-1440 minutes'') AND (gw.title LIKE ''OWNER-TASK%'' OR gw.title LIKE ''OWNER-NOTE%'')) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = p.id AND c.status IN (''active'',''holding'') AND COALESCE(c.last_verdict,'''') IN (''fail'',''vacuous-probe-result'',''probe-error'',''probe-not-machine-executable'',''probe-same-account-host''))', json_array('INSERT INTO issue_triage (issue_id, rc, triage_state, owner, sla_due_at, close_evidence) SELECT p.id, ''breach-doctor:PN-R2'', ''closed'', ''breach-doctor'', datetime(''now''), ''SUPERSEDED BY #'' || t.id || '': PROBE-NEEDED-1 asks for a closing probe of issue '' || t.id || '', an '' || CASE WHEN t.title LIKE ''OWNER-TASK%'' THEN ''OWNER-TASK'' ELSE ''OWNER-NOTE'' END || '' item whose definition of done is to act on it or record why not (belief belief-pn-r2-owner-outcome-unmeasured: no table records that outcome, so no probe can measure it). Issue '' || t.id || '' was open when this rule closed the PN and stays open. v_issue_dead_end lists it while it has no live contract. Closed by breach-doctor rule PN-R2 from ids and enum codes only.'' FROM agent_issues p JOIN agent_issues t ON t.id = CAST(substr(p.title, 23) AS INTEGER) WHERE p.id = ?1 AND p.status = ''open'' AND p.source = ''qnfo-fleet-control'' AND p.title LIKE ''PROBE-NEEDED-1: issue-%'' AND p.title = ''PROBE-NEEDED-1: issue-'' || CAST(substr(p.title, 23) AS INTEGER) AND t.status = ''open'' AND (t.title LIKE ''OWNER-TASK%'' OR t.title LIKE ''OWNER-NOTE%'') AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_lifecycle gl JOIN agent_issues gq ON gq.id = gl.issue_id JOIN agent_issues gw ON gw.id = CAST(substr(gq.title, 23) AS INTEGER) WHERE gq.title LIKE ''PROBE-NEEDED-1: issue-%'' AND gl.event IN (''opened'',''reopened'') AND gl.ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'',''-1440 minutes'') AND (gw.title LIKE ''OWNER-TASK%'' OR gw.title LIKE ''OWNER-NOTE%'')) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = p.id AND c.status IN (''active'',''holding'') AND COALESCE(c.last_verdict,'''') IN (''fail'',''vacuous-probe-result'',''probe-error'',''probe-not-machine-executable'',''probe-same-account-host'')) ON CONFLICT(issue_id) DO UPDATE SET rc = excluded.rc, triage_state = ''closed'', owner = ''breach-doctor'', close_evidence = excluded.close_evidence', 'UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = ''superseded'', last_verdict = ''superseded:pn-no-measurable-dod'', next_due_at = NULL WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND class = ''issue-'' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) AND status IN (''active'',''holding'',''probe-review-refused'') AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues p WHERE p.id = ?1 AND p.status IN (''closed'',''resolved''))'), json_array('UPDATE issue_triage SET triage_state = ''triaged'', close_evidence = NULL WHERE issue_id = ?1', 'UPDATE agent_issues SET status = ''open'', close_channel = NULL, updated_at = CAST(strftime(''%s'',''now'') AS INTEGER) * 1000 WHERE id = ?1 AND status = ''closed''', 'UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = ''active'', last_verdict = NULL, next_due_at = datetime(''now'') WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND class = ''issue-'' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) AND last_verdict = ''superseded:pn-no-measurable-dod'''), 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE id = ?1 AND status = ''open'') THEN ''pn-reopened'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed', 'delegated', 1, 12, 1, 'on', 'PROBE-NEEDED-1 for an OWNER-TASK or OWNER-NOTE target: the target''s definition of done is ''act on it or record why not'' and owner_prompts.status does not record it (131 of 135 closed or wontfix OWNER-TASK issues still read queued on 2026-10-26 12:15Z; belief belief-pn-r2-owner-outcome-unmeasured, with its falsifying probe), so no probe can measure it and a model-authored one would be vacuous. The PN is closed SUPERSEDED BY the target, which stays open and stays listed by fm-open-issue-no-doer and v_issue_dead_end while it has no live contract (13 of the 21 open owner items had none at 12:15Z): the rule takes the owner item out of the PROBE-NEEDED-1 queue and gives it no doer. GATE (control pn-r2-filer-quiet-gate): acts only when no PROBE-NEEDED-1 issue for such a target was opened or reopened in the last 1440 minutes (the filer''s own dedupe horizon: issue_refile_reopen reopens a PN closed within 24 hours and the filer files at most 12 PN per 1440 minutes; it is not a stuck-item SLA), because the filer (rtEnsureLivePath) re-files any orphan target and the D1 trigger issue_refile_reopen would reopen the PN within a tick of every close. The code lever that removes the cause is the issue BREACH-DOCTOR-1: PN-R2 qnfo-fleet-control (RT_LIVEPATH_ORPHAN_SQL excludes OWNER-TASK and OWNER-NOTE; the lever issue closes only when a code-read of main finds that exclusion, never on a quiet day), after which the gate opens by itself. max_per_tick is 1, so while the filer is still active (the gate opens only after 1440 minutes of quiet) the worst case is one close and one reopen a day. A close the filer undoes fails verify (pn-reopened) and shuts the gate again, and 2 such failures in 24 h demote the rule to measure in the engine. LIVE 2026-10-26 11:25Z: 7 candidate PNs (9 at 10:55Z), 0 hits because 6 class-C PN events were opened or reopened in the last 1440 minutes (gate closed).');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO breach_playbooks (rule_id, version, family, cause_class, action_kind, trigger_sql, action_sql, revert_sql, verify_sql, min_ladder, max_per_tick, max_per_day, enabled, mode, note) VALUES
  ('PN-R3', 1, 'PROBE-NEEDED-1', 'probe-review-refused', 'sql', 'SELECT p.id AS issue_id, ''probe-review-refused'' AS subject, json_object(''target_id'', CAST(substr(p.title, 23) AS INTEGER), ''contract_attempts'', c.attempts, ''contract_status'', c.status) AS facts_json FROM agent_issues p JOIN remediation_contracts c ON c.class = ''issue-'' || p.id WHERE p.status = ''open'' AND p.source = ''qnfo-fleet-control'' AND p.title LIKE ''PROBE-NEEDED-1: issue-%'' AND p.title = ''PROBE-NEEDED-1: issue-'' || CAST(substr(p.title, 23) AS INTEGER) AND c.status = ''probe-review-refused'' AND c.module = ''reopen-live-path'' AND c.verify_probe = (SELECT ''SELECT ''''ok'''' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues x WHERE x.id = '' || CAST(substr(pp.title, 23) AS INTEGER) || '' AND x.status = ''''open'''') THEN ''''ok'''' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = '' || CAST(substr(pp.title, 23) AS INTEGER) || '' AND c.status IN (''''active'''', ''''holding'''') AND instr(c.verify_probe, ''''needs-machine'''' || ''''-probe'''') = 0 AND instr(c.verify_probe, ''''SELECT status FROM agent_issues WHERE'''' || '''' id ='''') = 0 AND instr(c.verify_probe, ''''agent_issues WHERE id = '' || CAST(substr(pp.title, 23) AS INTEGER) || '')'''') = 0) THEN ''''ok'''' ELSE ''''pending: issue '' || CAST(substr(pp.title, 23) AS INTEGER) || '' has no probe of its own yet, a doer writes one'''' END AS observed'' FROM agent_issues pp WHERE pp.id = p.id)', json_array('UPDATE remediation_contracts SET module = ''probe-template-v4-pn'', status = ''active'', last_verdict = NULL, attempts = 0, deferred_since = NULL, next_due_at = datetime(''now'') WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND class = ''issue-'' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) AND status = ''probe-review-refused'' AND module = ''reopen-live-path'' AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues p WHERE p.id = ?1 AND p.status = ''open'' AND p.source = ''qnfo-fleet-control'' AND p.title LIKE ''PROBE-NEEDED-1: issue-%'' AND p.title = ''PROBE-NEEDED-1: issue-'' || CAST(substr(p.title, 23) AS INTEGER)) AND verify_probe = (SELECT ''SELECT ''''ok'''' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues x WHERE x.id = '' || CAST(substr(pp.title, 23) AS INTEGER) || '' AND x.status = ''''open'''') THEN ''''ok'''' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = '' || CAST(substr(pp.title, 23) AS INTEGER) || '' AND c.status IN (''''active'''', ''''holding'''') AND instr(c.verify_probe, ''''needs-machine'''' || ''''-probe'''') = 0 AND instr(c.verify_probe, ''''SELECT status FROM agent_issues WHERE'''' || '''' id ='''') = 0 AND instr(c.verify_probe, ''''agent_issues WHERE id = '' || CAST(substr(pp.title, 23) AS INTEGER) || '')'''') = 0) THEN ''''ok'''' ELSE ''''pending: issue '' || CAST(substr(pp.title, 23) AS INTEGER) || '' has no probe of its own yet, a doer writes one'''' END AS observed'' FROM agent_issues pp WHERE pp.id = ?1)'), json_array('UPDATE remediation_contracts SET module = ''reopen-live-path'', status = ''probe-review-refused'', last_verdict = ''probe-review-refused'', next_due_at = NULL WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND class = ''issue-'' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) AND module = ''probe-template-v4-pn'''), 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE id = ?1 AND status = ''open'') THEN ''ok'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.class = ''issue-'' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) AND c.module = ''probe-template-v4-pn'' AND c.status IN (''active'',''holding'')) THEN ''ok'' ELSE ''still-refused'' END AS observed', 'delegated', 6, 25, 1, 'on', 'qnfo-cloud-ops PROBE-REVIEW-1 asks a model to judge every d1-query contract on an open issue and skips module probe-template%, so it refused the fleet''s own deterministic PROBE-NEEDED-1 probe (text of rtLivePathProbe) on some issues and passed the identical text on others (17 of 53 open PN contracts refused on 2026-10-26 05:45Z, and neither executor reads a refused contract). The row restores status active with the module swap probe-template-v4-pn, which PROBE-REVIEW-1 skips, so it is not refused again. Exact text equality with rtLivePathProbe(target) is the guard: only the fleet''s own template is restored, never a probe a session wrote. qnfo-cloud-ops PROBE_REVIEW_SELECT is not touched (claimed by another session). New PN contracts are still born with module reopen-live-path, so this stays a standing rule: a refusal is repaired once the PN is older than the doctor''s age gate (breach_doctor_min_age_min, 60 minutes). LIVE 2026-10-26 11:25Z: 4 hits (PN 1000088, 1000396, 100415, 100534, each with the exact rtLivePathProbe text), 6 at 10:55Z (PN 1000175 and 100559 closed since).');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO breach_playbooks (rule_id, version, family, cause_class, action_kind, trigger_sql, action_sql, revert_sql, verify_sql, min_ladder, max_per_tick, max_per_day, enabled, mode, note) VALUES
  ('PB-R0', 1, 'BORN-SUPERSEDED', 'real-probe-superseded', 'sql', 'SELECT a.id AS issue_id, ''real-probe-superseded'' AS subject, json_object(''own_attempts'', c.attempts, ''probe_chars'', length(c.verify_probe)) AS facts_json FROM agent_issues a JOIN remediation_contracts c ON c.class = ''issue-'' || a.id AND c.issue_id = a.id WHERE a.status = ''open'' AND c.status = ''superseded'' AND c.last_verdict LIKE ''superseded:closure-observing-probe-at-birth%'' AND upper(trim(c.verify_probe)) LIKE ''SELECT%'' AND c.verify_transport LIKE ''d1-query%'' AND instr(lower(c.verify_probe), ''expected'') > 0 AND instr(lower(c.verify_probe), ''observed'') > 0 AND instr(lower(c.verify_probe), ''agent_issues'') = 0 AND instr(lower(c.verify_probe), ''issue_triage'') = 0 AND instr(lower(c.verify_probe), ''issue_lifecycle'') = 0 AND instr(lower(c.verify_probe), ''close_evidence'') = 0 AND instr(lower(c.verify_probe), ''remediation_contracts'') = 0 AND instr(lower(c.verify_probe), ''remediation_verifications'') = 0 AND instr(c.verify_probe, ''needs-machine'' || ''-probe'') = 0 AND lower(c.verify_probe) NOT LIKE ''%id = '' || a.id || ''%'' AND lower(c.verify_probe) NOT LIKE ''%issue_id = '' || a.id || ''%'' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts d WHERE d.issue_id = a.id AND d.status IN (''active'',''holding''))', json_array('UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = ''active'', module = ''breach-doctor-restored'', last_verdict = NULL, attempts = 0, deferred_since = NULL, next_due_at = datetime(''now''), expected_cadence_h = 1 WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND class = ''issue-'' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) AND status = ''superseded'' AND last_verdict LIKE ''superseded:closure-observing-probe-at-birth%'' AND upper(trim(verify_probe)) LIKE ''SELECT%'' AND verify_transport LIKE ''d1-query%'' AND instr(lower(verify_probe), ''expected'') > 0 AND instr(lower(verify_probe), ''observed'') > 0 AND instr(lower(verify_probe), ''agent_issues'') = 0 AND instr(lower(verify_probe), ''issue_triage'') = 0 AND instr(lower(verify_probe), ''issue_lifecycle'') = 0 AND instr(lower(verify_probe), ''close_evidence'') = 0 AND instr(lower(verify_probe), ''remediation_contracts'') = 0 AND instr(lower(verify_probe), ''remediation_verifications'') = 0 AND instr(verify_probe, ''needs-machine'' || ''-probe'') = 0 AND lower(verify_probe) NOT LIKE ''%id = '' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) || ''%'' AND lower(verify_probe) NOT LIKE ''%issue_id = '' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) || ''%'' AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues a WHERE a.id = ?1 AND a.status = ''open'') AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts d WHERE d.issue_id = ?1 AND d.status IN (''active'',''holding''))'), json_array('UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = ''superseded'', module = ''probe-template-v3-generic'', last_verdict = ''superseded:closure-observing-probe-at-birth (restored by breach-doctor rule PB-R0, then reverted)'', next_due_at = NULL WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND class = ''issue-'' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) AND module = ''breach-doctor-restored'' AND status IN (''active'',''holding'')'), 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE id = ?1 AND status = ''open'') THEN ''ok'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.class = ''issue-'' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) AND c.status IN (''active'',''holding'')) THEN ''ok'' ELSE ''still-superseded'' END AS observed', 'delegated', 6, 12, 1, 'on', 'CLOSE-PROBE-CIRCULAR-1 (trigger contract_probe_templates_v3_generic) supersedes the birth contract of an issue whose probe observed the guarded issue''s own status. 104 of the 110 open issues in that state were judged correctly. Six were not: their probe measures a real condition (METRIC-UNMEASURED-1 issues 1000384 to 1000389 read metric_improvement_now rows per owner). The row restores a superseded-at-birth contract (status active, last_verdict NULL, attempts 0, next_due_at now) only when its probe is a SELECT returning expected and observed, references none of agent_issues, issue_triage, issue_lifecycle, close_evidence, remediation_contracts or remediation_verifications, does not carry the issue id as a literal, and the issue has no active or holding contract. LIVE 2026-10-26 11:25Z: 0 hits (the six were restored in the meantime: contracts active, verdict fail from the 10:18Z executor read), so this row is the standing guard for the next one. MODULE: the restored contract takes module breach-doctor-restored, not the probe-template-v3-generic it was born with, because qnfo-cloud-ops PROBE_REVIEW_SELECT skips every module LIKE probe-template% and this rule''s test of a real probe is syntactic: the restored probe stays in the model reviewer''s selection, which catches a self-confirming or vacuous one. The revert puts the old module back.');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO breach_playbooks (rule_id, version, family, cause_class, action_kind, trigger_sql, action_sql, revert_sql, verify_sql, min_ladder, max_per_tick, max_per_day, enabled, mode, note) VALUES
  ('PB-T1', 1, 'PORTFOLIO-GAP', 'portfolio-gap-orphan', 'sql', 'SELECT x.id AS issue_id, ''portfolio-gap'' AS subject, json_object(''gap_rows'', (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM portfolio_gaps g WHERE g.issue_id = x.id), ''gap_open'', (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM portfolio_gaps g WHERE g.issue_id = x.id AND g.status = ''open''), ''own_contract'', COALESCE((SELECT c.status FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.class = ''issue-'' || x.id), ''none'')) AS facts_json FROM (SELECT a.id AS id FROM agent_issues a WHERE a.title LIKE ''PORTFOLIO-GAP %'' AND a.status = ''open'' AND a.title NOT LIKE ''PROBE-NEEDED-1: issue-%'' AND a.title NOT LIKE ''OWNER-TASK%'' AND a.title NOT LIKE ''OWNER-NOTE%'' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = a.id AND c.status IN (''active'',''holding'',''monitoring'',''escalated'') AND c.class NOT LIKE ''%-BACKFILL-1'' AND instr(lower(c.verify_probe), ''close_evidence'') = 0) AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM portfolio_gaps g WHERE g.issue_id = a.id)) x WHERE 1 = 1 AND NOT ((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM portfolio_gaps g WHERE g.issue_id = x.id AND g.status = ''open'') = 0)', json_array('UPDATE remediation_contracts SET verify_probe = ''SELECT ''''resolved'''' AS expected, CASE WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM portfolio_gaps WHERE issue_id = '' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) || '') = 0 THEN ''''pending: no gap row carries issue '' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) || '''''' WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM portfolio_gaps WHERE issue_id = '' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) || '' AND status = ''''open'''') = 0 THEN ''''resolved'''' ELSE ''''pending: '''' || (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM portfolio_gaps WHERE issue_id = '' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) || '' AND status = ''''open'''') || '''' of '''' || (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM portfolio_gaps WHERE issue_id = '' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) || '') || '''' gap rows still open'''' END AS observed'', verify_transport = ''d1-query'', status = ''active'', module = ''probe-template-v4-portfolio-gap'', last_verdict = NULL, attempts = 0, deferred_since = NULL, next_due_at = datetime(''now''), expected_cadence_h = 1, precondition = ''PROBE-PLAYBOOKS-1 template portfolio-gap: the portfolio_gaps rows that carry this issue are its definition of done'', action = ''the portfolio autopilot closes the gap rows (portfolio_gaps.status open to closed or resolved), the probe reads them and a pass closes the issue'' WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND class = ''issue-'' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) AND (status IN (''superseded'',''probe-review-refused'',''needs-machine-probe'') OR (status IN (''active'',''holding'',''monitoring'',''escalated'') AND instr(lower(verify_probe), ''close_evidence'') > 0)) AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues a WHERE a.id = ?1 AND a.title LIKE ''PORTFOLIO-GAP %'' AND a.status = ''open'' AND a.title NOT LIKE ''PROBE-NEEDED-1: issue-%'' AND a.title NOT LIKE ''OWNER-TASK%'' AND a.title NOT LIKE ''OWNER-NOTE%'' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = a.id AND c.status IN (''active'',''holding'',''monitoring'',''escalated'') AND c.class NOT LIKE ''%-BACKFILL-1'' AND instr(lower(c.verify_probe), ''close_evidence'') = 0) AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM portfolio_gaps g WHERE g.issue_id = a.id) AND 1 = 1 AND NOT ((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM portfolio_gaps g WHERE g.issue_id = a.id AND g.status = ''open'') = 0))', 'UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = ''superseded'', last_verdict = ''superseded:circular-backfill-replaced'', next_due_at = NULL WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND class LIKE ''%-BACKFILL-1'' AND status IN (''active'',''holding'',''probe-review-refused'',''needs-machine-probe'') AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts n WHERE n.class = ''issue-'' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) AND n.module = ''probe-template-v4-portfolio-gap'' AND n.status IN (''active'',''holding''))'), json_array('UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = ''superseded'', module = ''probe-template-v3-generic'', last_verdict = ''superseded:closure-observing-probe-at-birth (installed by breach-doctor rule PB-T1, then reverted)'', next_due_at = NULL WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND class = ''issue-'' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) AND module = ''probe-template-v4-portfolio-gap''', 'UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = ''active'', last_verdict = NULL, next_due_at = datetime(''now'') WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND class LIKE ''%-BACKFILL-1'' AND last_verdict = ''superseded:circular-backfill-replaced'''), 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE id = ?1 AND status = ''open'') THEN ''ok'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.class = ''issue-'' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) AND c.module = ''probe-template-v4-portfolio-gap'' AND c.status IN (''active'',''holding'')) THEN ''ok'' ELSE ''no-live-template'' END AS observed', 'delegated', 6, 30, 1, 'on', 'PORTFOLIO-GAP issue with no live closing path (its birth contract was superseded as circular, a BACKFILL-1 alias or a refused probe): install template T1 on its own contract, the probe reads the portfolio_gaps rows that carry the issue (portfolio_gaps.issue_id) and is ok when none is still open, and supersede a BACKFILL-1 alias only after the template is live (R7). Template text tested read-only on live qnfo-audit (issue 100341: pending 7 of 7 gap rows still open). Pending form: the probe reads pending now, so the contract is installed active and the executor reads it within the hour. LIVE 2026-10-26 11:25Z: 1 hit (PORTFOLIO-GAP 1000125, 2 of 2 gap rows open). 11 at 10:55Z: the other ten were given a live contract by another loop in between.');

