  'Pillar autonomy. Read: SELECT family, cause_class, state, COUNT(*) FROM v_breach_diagnosis_current WHERE rule_id LIKE ''PB-%'' OR rule_id LIKE ''PN-%'' GROUP BY 1, 2, 3; the open issues counted are the ones the PB-R0 and PB-T rows of breach_playbooks do not match: SELECT a.id, a.title, a.source FROM agent_issues a WHERE a.status = ''open'' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = a.id AND c.status IN (''active'',''holding'',''monitoring'',''escalated'') AND c.class NOT LIKE ''%-BACKFILL-1'' AND instr(lower(c.verify_probe), ''close_evidence'') = 0). Lever: a breach_playbooks row for the largest unmatched title family by migration (trigger_sql returns issue_id, subject, facts_json, see migrations/2026-10-26-probe-playbooks.sql for the template shape), or the probe author (rtAuthorLivePathProbe) for prose definitions of done. Done when the metric reads 0 for 3 ticks.',
